# Periodic safety-snapshot checkpoints written by projected_rk4_integrate.m
# during long runs -- transient, regenerable, overwritten every run, no
# standalone diagnostic value (unlike the p*_result.mat / phase_b*_result.mat
# files, which ARE evidence cited in docs/HANDOFF.md and should stay tracked).
projected_rk4_checkpoint.mat
c0_checkpoint_test.mat

# Phase C production run output (Phase C.0 gate round 6 close-out, GPT
# audit): the durable run-and-save wrapper (run_phase_c.m ->
# paper1608/simulation/run_phase_c_production.m) writes its result,
# manifest, and console log under artifacts/work/phase-c/. Kept OUTSIDE
# git tracking on purpose
# so `git status` stays clean while the wrapper's own git_fingerprint()
# checks are sampled during a multi-hour run -- durable on disk (not
# deleted), just not committed. Review and selectively copy/commit
# specific files (e.g. the manifest) after the run, if wanted.
artifacts/work/

# Legacy working-output location retained so older local launch commands do
# not accidentally add generated production data to version control.
phase_c_results/
